From: Yeison Delgado <yeisonestivendelgado109@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:03:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(device): active low-energy alerts for Falcon and SMAC
 (F-44, F-45)

GET /device/low-energy lists one LOW_ENERGY alert per device of the user
scope whose latest stored supercaps_per (Falcon) or battery_per (SMAC) is
below its threshold (FALCON_LOW_ENERGY_PERCENT / SMAC_LOW_ENERGY_PERCENT,
30 % by default). A reading at or above the threshold clears it. Each alert
carries the level, the threshold, the reading time and since, the first
reading of the current low streak. Lowest level first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012Za94ATKRpuhbxLyQmG5TG
